notifyT -- which writes tell a field's listeners (Tony, 2026-11-12, SEQ 629: arithmetic writes notify, guarded, with a
re-entry guard). One listener per notifier; each listener's action bumps a counter, zeroed before each write.

fires     every write that changes a value: =, +=, *=, /=, ++ and -- (prefix), on a count and on a number; text = and +=;
          := on a holder. Before this stroke count += *= ++ -- and number += *= fired nothing: they write the raw count
          or number, and only the setters called updateListeners.
quiet     +% (an attach) and :. (a flag) change no value and fire nothing.
minus     CURED 2026-11-12 (Tony): -= on a listened-to field subtracts and fires once. opMinusEQ used to ask whether the
          target held any list, and the listener list is an attribute, so it took the remove-a-member arm. It now asks
          for members only. Before the cure this line read: fired 0, value 31.
reentry   a listener whose action writes its own notifier (with = and with +=) fires once per outside write and the run
          ends: updateListeners takes hasListeners down for its walk. H7 (run under an alarm, 2026-11-12): with the two hasListeners lines out of updateListeners the run dies, exit 139, before any reentry line.
jitted    CURED 2026-11-12 (Tony: a jitted write fires once per write, as the interpreter's does). jWrite makes four writes,
          = += -= and ++, and its listener fires four times jitted, on a refire, and interpreted. Before the cure the
          compiled = stored straight into the field and told nobody; only the += (which runs the operator) fired.
